    {
     "k": "finance.faq.0.q",
     "t": "text",
     "l": "Question 1",
     "v": "Can I get finance approved before choosing a car?"
    },
    {
     "k": "finance.faq.0.a",
     "t": "text",
     "l": "Answer 1",
     "v": "Yes, and it is the better order. A pre-approval tells you your real budget including the on-road price, so you are choosing a car you can actually drive away rather than one you can nearly afford."
    },
    {
     "k": "finance.faq.1.q",
     "t": "text",
     "l": "Question 2",
     "v": "Do you charge for arranging finance?"
    },
    {
     "k": "finance.faq.1.a",
     "t": "text",
     "l": "Answer 2",
     "v": "No. The lender pays a standard commission and it does not change your rate. We show you every offer we receive, including the ones that pay us less."
    },
    {
     "k": "finance.faq.2.q",
     "t": "text",
     "l": "Question 3",
     "v": "Can I foreclose the loan early?"
    },
    {
     "k": "finance.faq.2.a",
     "t": "text",
     "l": "Answer 3",
     "v": "Terms vary by lender. Some allow it free after twelve EMIs, others charge a percentage of the outstanding. It is on the comparison sheet — read that column before you sign, not after."
    },
    {
     "k": "finance.faq.3.q",
     "t": "text",
     "l": "Question 4",
     "v": "Is finance available on True Value cars?"
    },
    {
     "k": "finance.faq.3.a",
     "t": "text",
     "l": "Answer 4",
     "v": "Yes, though rates are typically higher than on a new car and the maximum tenure is shorter. We will show you both so you can compare properly."
    }
